  "tpdc_english_documentation": {
    "id": "4ae6383f-17a0-48ed-8b68-7d6a5439dab2",
    "metadataId": "2f302c7f-00bc-4ace-af30-5fa9277ed16e",
    "title": "Global gapless 1 km daily mean land surface temperature dataset (2003-2023)",
    "description": "Daily mean land surface temperature (LST) is a key variable in land–atmosphere interactions, hydrological balance, and climate change. However, satellite thermal infrared-derived LSTs are often affected by cloud contamination, resulting in substantial data gaps that hinder daily mean LST compositing. Regarding this, we develop a three-step framework: (1) estimating gapped daily mean LSTs via empirical linear combinations of four daily MODIS observations; (2) reconstructing preliminary gapless daily mean LSTs using the semi-physical enhanced annual temperature cycle model and weighted spatial interpolation; and (3) optimizing the final gapless daily mean LSTs through an XGBoost learning scheme that incorporates in situ measurements and auxiliary variables. A global gapless 1 km daily mean LST dataset was generated spanning 2003–2023. Validation against worldwide in situ observations demonstrates the product achieving an overall RMSE of 1.838 K (daily) and independent accuracies of 2.073 K (daily) and 1.511 K (monthly). ",
    "language": "en",
    "userLimit": null,
    "instructions": "File naming: The daily mean land surface temperature is stored in .tif format and named as \"yyyy_mm_dd_DMLST.tif\", where yyyy, mm, and dd represent the year, month, and day, respectively.\nUsage: The .tif files in this dataset can be read using Python, IDL, and other tools. The data type is Int16, with a scale factor of 0.01.",
    "useTerms": "To respect the intellectual property rights, protect the rights of data authors, expand services of the data center, and evaluate the application potential of data, data users should clearly indicate the source of the data and the author of the data in the research results generated by using the data (including published papers, articles, data products, and unpublished research reports, data products and other results). For re-posting (second or multiple releases) data, the author must also indicate the source of the original data.",
